course: dictionary
lesson: 14716
title: Prod: poke or nudge
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word prod can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to prod means to poke something with a finger, a stick or another pointed thing. It can also mean to push someone gently to do something they are slow to do. «Mum had to prod Sam to start his homework.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. If someone is poking, there will be a finger, a stick or something pointy nearby. If someone is slow, there will be a reason to push them on. «The doctor prodded my tummy gently to find where it hurt.» The doctor is checking, not being rude.
explain: As a noun, a prod is a poke, or a reminder. «Nadia gave her brother a prod, and he woke up.» Notice the spelling: prod, prods, prodded, prodding. Use prodded for something that already happened.
fact: Prod means to poke someone or something with a finger, a stick or another pointed thing.
fact: Prod can also mean to push or remind someone to do something they are slow to do.
fact: As a noun, a prod is a poke, or a reminder. You can say «give someone a prod».
fact: «Prod at» means to poke again and again at something.
fact: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence: «Mum had to remind Sam to start his homework» still makes sense, so prod fits.
exercise: «Ben used a stick to prod the sleeping dog.» What does prod mean here? | *To poke with a stick | To sing loudly | To hug gently | To tie a knot
exercise: Mum says, «Can you give Sam a prod? He is still in bed.» What does a prod mean? | *A poke, or a reminder to get moving | A loud shout across the house | To sleep for hours | A new bed
exercise: What kind of word is prod in «She gave her brother a prod»? | A verb | An adjective | A full stop | *A noun
test: «The doctor gently prodded my tummy to find the sore spot.» What does prodded mean? | Tickled | *Poked or pressed with a finger | Measured with a ruler | Kissed
test: «Leo kept prodding at the ice on the pond with a stick.» What does prodding at mean? | Covering it with snow | Skating across it | Singing to it | *Poking again and again
exam: Jayden says, «A quick prod from Dad got me out of bed.» What does a prod mean here? | A new pair of shoes | *A poke or reminder that gets you moving | A quiet song | A big meal
